That can't be the same Vice Warden I know.

523
00:31:53,780 --> 00:31:54,610
Move!

524
00:31:55,380 --> 00:31:57,057
Try and make me!

525
00:31:57,140 --> 00:31:59,657
He actually knows what he's doing.

526
00:31:59,740 --> 00:32:02,799
And here, I thought he was
only good at complaining.

527
00:32:13,920 --> 00:32:15,000
What? HENYA!

528
00:32:23,280 --> 00:32:25,657
That's right, the HENYA Hustle Dance!

529
00:32:25,740 --> 00:32:27,480
Infernal Hell Wheel!

530
00:32:37,200 --> 00:32:39,820
Get the hell out of my way! I'll make you!

531
00:32:39,940 --> 00:32:40,940
I gotta save him!

532
00:32:41,080 --> 00:32:42,280
You gotta be joking!

533
00:32:42,560 --> 00:32:47,384
What kind of vice-war would I be if I
stepped aside just cause an inmate asked me?

534
00:33:00,220 --> 00:33:01,800
Second gear!

535
00:33:02,420 --> 00:33:04,360
Now come, come!

536
00:33:05,160 --> 00:33:06,320
Get off!

537
00:33:06,800 --> 00:33:07,760
Get away!

538
00:33:28,160 --> 00:33:30,042
We've been praying you'd arrive.

539
00:33:31,240 --> 00:33:33,828
You've got to do
something, Warden Magellan.

540
00:33:43,920 --> 00:33:46,537
Where are the ringleaders
behind this uprising?

541
00:33:46,620 --> 00:33:48,857
They're in front of the
staircase to level three,

542
00:33:48,940 --> 00:33:51,277
but that's on the opposite
side of the floor from here?

543
00:33:51,360 --> 00:33:53,217
and we're going to have to
fight our way through the riot.

544
00:33:53,300 --> 00:33:56,940
So far, Vice Warden
Hannibal has kept him back.

545
00:33:57,200 --> 00:33:59,259
Who knows how long he can hold out?

546
00:34:00,180 --> 00:34:01,820
No, Vice Warden!

547
00:34:08,120 --> 00:34:09,320
Let go!

548
00:34:12,420 --> 00:34:14,620
I'm not through with you yet!

549
00:34:23,580 --> 00:34:34,160
You won't pass!

550
00:34:39,520 --> 00:34:41,800
Follow the vice warden's lead.

551
00:34:42,080 --> 00:34:43,180
Don't hold back.

552
00:34:56,440 --> 00:34:59,720
You should worry about
saving your own life!

553
00:35:01,380 --> 00:35:02,380
Out of my way!

554
00:35:08,300 --> 00:35:09,220
Bastard.

555
00:35:09,900 --> 00:35:12,200
You are not getting past me!

556
00:35:13,520 --> 00:35:17,100
Shams of Jet Tail!

557
00:35:23,700 --> 00:35:24,780
Don't move!

558
00:35:25,840 --> 00:35:27,120
Just quit already!

559
00:35:28,160 --> 00:35:28,990
Dammit!

560
00:35:29,073 --> 00:35:30,822
I don't have time for this crap!

561
00:35:41,640 --> 00:35:45,934
You keep saying you want to save your
brother like it's some noble quest,

562
00:35:46,120 --> 00:35:48,179
but I know you're nothing but scum!

563
00:35:48,300 --> 00:35:49,140
Both of you!

564
00:35:54,440 --> 00:35:59,740
All the pirates and rebels here, you don't
give a damn about anyone but yourselves.

565
00:36:00,240 --> 00:36:02,500
Stop by swarting you've done enough!

566
00:36:02,940 --> 00:36:03,917
Don't stand up!

567
00:36:04,000 --> 00:36:05,097
You're gonna get killed!

568
00:36:05,180 --> 00:36:08,474
As long as scum like you are
free to terrorize the seas,

569
00:36:08,720 --> 00:36:10,857
decent people can't even
sleep at night because

570
00:36:10,940 --> 00:36:13,217
they're worried about
losing their loved ones.

571
00:36:13,300 --> 00:36:15,920
This jail was built to protect them.

572
00:36:16,320 --> 00:36:20,277
Locking up evil criminals like you is the
only way to give them some peace of mind.

573
00:36:20,360 --> 00:36:23,260
This fortress is the floodgate of hell!

574
00:36:23,640 --> 00:36:27,697
And I won't let the world drown in
terror by letting prisoners break free!

575
00:36:27,780 --> 00:36:31,800
So like I already said, you
won't take a single step!

576
00:36:34,280 --> 00:36:35,360
Bye, sport!

577
00:36:53,340 --> 00:36:56,940
The only thing I want is to
save my brother, so move it!

578
00:36:57,840 --> 00:36:59,605
You're too dumb to understand.

579
00:37:01,720 --> 00:37:03,880
I started, help us!

580
00:37:10,300 --> 00:37:11,130
Hey!

581
00:37:11,213 --> 00:37:12,649
What's happening in there?

582
00:37:12,780 --> 00:37:14,251
Buttercork in it already!

583
00:37:17,420 --> 00:37:21,067
All this blathering about what's
right and wrong in the world.

584
00:37:22,120 --> 00:37:25,473
If you'd look at the world
from outside your damn prison,

585
00:37:25,760 --> 00:37:27,820
it seems not so black and white.

586
00:37:29,020 --> 00:37:30,400
So cut the crap.

587
00:37:42,900 --> 00:37:43,760
That guy.

588
00:37:44,020 --> 00:37:45,180
I met him in Jaya!

589
00:37:58,660 --> 00:38:00,380
Oh, wow! Wow!

590
00:38:01,640 --> 00:38:04,560
Well, ain't this a fine
trip down memory lane!

591
00:38:06,240 --> 00:38:09,769
Looks like we got you boys right
in the middle of something!

592
00:38:11,980 --> 00:38:12,877
Hello, Teach.

593
00:38:12,960 --> 00:38:15,784
Mind telling us what the
hell you're doing here?

594
00:38:16,380 --> 00:38:19,800
Well, or do you only
answer to Blackbeard now?

595
00:38:21,960 --> 00:38:22,790
Jinbei.

596
00:38:24,660 --> 00:38:26,778
Hey, hey, what's with the hostility?

597
00:38:26,900 --> 00:38:29,297
Why don't you loosen up those fists there?

598
00:38:29,380 --> 00:38:32,300
Oh, yeah, I forgot you
and Ace are pretty tight.

599
00:38:32,500 --> 00:38:36,029
But hey, there's not much point
in caring about him anymore.

600
00:38:41,520 --> 00:38:42,350
Blackbeard.

601
00:38:42,840 --> 00:38:44,160
I can't right now.

602
00:38:44,260 --> 00:38:45,436
I'm chasing someone.

603
00:38:47,220 --> 00:38:49,200
He's a pirate named Blackbeard.

604
00:38:49,380 --> 00:38:54,060
The dreams of pirates will never end!

605
00:38:54,720 --> 00:38:55,617
According to this,

606
00:38:55,700 --> 00:38:59,717
a pirate named Blackbeard defeated Ace
and gave him up to the world government.

607
00:38:59,800 --> 00:39:02,388
In return, they invited
him to be a warlord.

608
00:39:05,740 --> 00:39:06,681
Blackbeard, huh?

609
00:39:10,280 --> 00:39:11,320
I see...

610
00:39:17,300 --> 00:39:18,340
So you're...

611
00:39:19,760 --> 00:39:20,590
Blackbeard!

612
00:39:20,900 --> 00:39:22,380
Huh? Oh, right.

613
00:39:22,620 --> 00:39:24,973
I guess I never gave you my name, did I?

614
00:39:27,180 --> 00:39:29,720
Long time no C, Straw Hat Luffy.

615
00:39:30,720 --> 00:39:32,340
Hey, I know how you feel.

616
00:39:32,540 --> 00:39:36,637
I was surprised myself when I heard you
were my old commander's baby brother.

617
00:39:36,720 --> 00:39:38,217
What are you doing down here?

618
00:39:38,300 --> 00:39:41,037
You're gonna miss the
big show don't you want

619
00:39:41,120 --> 00:39:43,944
to be there for your
brother's public execution?
